{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — GOOGLE STORE WIDGET (Google Customer Reviews badge) 2026-08-26 ═══

  WHAT THIS IS
  Google's official "store widget" — the current replacement for the Google
  Customer Reviews badge. It surfaces the store's Google rating, review count
  and Store Quality standing. The script URL and the start() call are verbatim
  from Google's own documentation:
      https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/14632921
  Do not retype either from memory.

  WHAT THIS IS **NOT** — read before adding anything else here
  This is NOT the survey opt-in module. The opt-in is the half that actually
  COLLECTS reviews, it is REQUIRED to take part in Google Customer Reviews, and
  Google requires it on the ORDER CONFIRMATION page carrying real order data:
  order id, customer email, delivery country, estimated delivery date.

  On Shopify that page is the Thank You page, and as of **26 August 2026**
  non-Plus stores can no longer put scripts on it — checkout.liquid, the
  Additional Scripts box and ScriptTags were all removed for Thank You and
  Order Status pages on that date. This theme contains no file that renders
  there (there is no checkout.liquid and no thank-you template — verified).
  The opt-in is therefore enabled in the **Google & YouTube app**, not here.

  Do NOT paste the opt-in snippet into this theme to "make it work". On a
  storefront page there is no order to report, so it would hand Google an
  order_id and delivery date for an order that does not exist.

  NO merchant_id IS PASSED, AND THAT IS CORRECT
  The current widget identifies the store by the domain it runs on, which must
  be claimed in Merchant Center. The retired badge took merchant_id; this one
  does not accept it. Adding one is not a harmless extra — it is not part of
  the documented API.

  PLACEMENT — MEASURED, NOT GUESSED
  LEFT_BOTTOM rather than Google's RIGHT_BOTTOM default, because the right
  corner is already occupied on every template:
      .wa-float   position:fixed bottom:24px right:24px   layout/theme.liquid:852
      .waf        position:fixed bottom:24px right:24px   templates/index.liquid:575
  WhatsApp contact is a GA4 key event for this store. A Google badge parked on
  top of that button would cost real conversations. CSS `right` is physical, so
  this holds even though the site is dir="rtl".

  On a PRODUCT page the whole bottom edge is spoken for by the sticky
  add-to-cart bar — .pdp-sticky, position:fixed bottom:0 inset-inline:0,
  z-index:98, switched on at max-width:900px
  (templates/product.liquid:485 and :533). It spans the FULL width, so neither
  corner is safe there. Google picks its own "mobile" breakpoint, which we do
  not control and which need not agree with 900px, so its margin options cannot
  be trusted to clear the bar. The widget is simply not started on a product
  page below 900px. Above 900px .pdp-sticky is display:none and the corner is
  free.

  DUPLICATION GUARD
  Enabling "Store widgets" inside the Google & YouTube app may later make the
  app inject this same script. Two live copies would mean two badges, so the
  script is injected only when no other copy is present. Whichever arrives
  first wins. (Measured 2026-08-26: the storefront carried no merchantwidget.js,
  so there is nothing to collide with today.)

  IF THE STORE IS NOT ELIGIBLE, NOTHING RENDERS
  The widget only paints once Merchant Center holds a Store Quality rating for
  the domain. Until then this is a silent no-op — it does not draw an empty,
  broken or placeholder badge. No layout shift either way: the widget is
  position:fixed and never occupies document flow.

  TO TURN IT OFF: set the flag below to false.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign show_google_store_widget = true -%}

{%- if show_google_store_widget -%}
<script>
(function () {
  var SRC = 'https://www.gstatic.com/shopping/merchant/merchantwidget.js';

  /* never run a second copy alongside one the Google & YouTube app injected */
  if (window.merchantwidget || document.querySelector('script[src*="merchantwidget.js"]')) return;

  {%- if template.name == 'product' %}
  /* the sticky add-to-cart bar owns the bottom edge below 900px — see comment above */
  if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 900px)').matches) return;
  {%- endif %}

  var s = document.createElement('script');
  s.id = 'merchantWidgetScript';
  s.src = SRC;
  s.defer = true;
  s.addEventListener('load', function () {
    if (typeof merchantwidget === 'undefined') return;
    merchantwidget.start({
      position: 'LEFT_BOTTOM'
    });
  });
  document.head.appendChild(s);
})();
</script>
{%- endif -%}
